  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You conjure a claw-footed cauldron full of bubbling liquid in an unoccupied space on the ground within 5 feet of you. It lasts for the duration, can’t be moved, and vanishes with its contents when the spell ends.</p><p>The liquid duplicates the properties of a Common or an Uncommon potion of your choice (such as a Potion of Healing). As a Bonus Action, you or an ally can reach into the cauldron and draw out one potion of that kind, in a vial that vanishes once the potion is consumed. The cauldron can produce a number of potions equal to your spellcasting ability modifier (minimum 1); when the last one is drawn, the cauldron disappears and the spell ends.</p><p>Potions from the cauldron that haven’t been consumed vanish when you cast this spell again.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-x8lwaAYqjOYIZ9wa\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Drag the chosen potion onto the sheets of those who draw one, and delete them when the spell is cast again.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
